Package: janus
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Janus contributors <janus@localhost.invalid>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Depends: @SHLIBDEPS@, libvulkan1, libwayland-client0, fontconfig, pipewire, xdg-desktop-portal, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-kde, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, mesa-va-drivers, mesa-vulkan-drivers
Suggests: intel-media-va-driver
Description: Native desktop casting application
 Janus discovers TVs and screens on the local network and casts the whole
 screen or one application window, with optional desktop sound, speaking each
 receiver's own protocol (Google Cast, AirPlay, Hisense/EShare boards).
 .
 H.264 is encoded on the GPU through GStreamer's VA plugin when the graphics
 driver supports it; otherwise Janus uses its built-in software encoder.
